WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.434
Host: Compare nutrient handling after a meal
and during fasting.

2
00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:10.457
Guide: The fed state favours use and storage
of absorbed nutrients under a higher insulin
signal.

3
00:00:10.457 --> 00:00:18.400
Guide: Fasting promotes mobilisation of stored
fuels and hepatic glucose production under a
lower insulin-to-glucagon signal.

4
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.084
Guide: Energy is transferred and transformed,
not created.

5
00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:27.802
Host: Which statement best connects fasting to
ongoing cellular work?

6
00:00:27.802 --> 00:00:32.706
Guide: Stored substrates are mobilised to
support continued metabolism.

7
00:00:32.706 --> 00:00:37.825
Guide: Fasting changes fuel sources while
tissues continue to use energy.
